body: "## Observed release failure (not a compromise claim)\nThe resumed release published `pm-ops@2026.11.11` to npm, then refused its provenance because the expected signer identity came from the preparation run rather than the publishing job.\n\n- [Publishing run 43272393997 / job 131409063583](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/43272393997/job/131409063583), completed with failure, publishes merged commit `20aeecbd83f6d997576903c881940d459c9b5042`.\n- Job reports reusable workflow `daily-release.yml@refs/heads/main (20aeec...)`; trusted verifier checkout also resolves **20aeec**, not the preparation revision.\n- Candidate preparation run `43010127872/attempts/1` and tools pin are `831a0f01400ed352b75f01ed8ecf6e05b1308fe3`.\n- Job environment sets `PROVENANCE_SIGNER_WORKFLOW=unbraind/pm-ops/.github/workflows/daily-release.yml@831a0f01400ed352b75f01ed8ecf6e05b1308fe3`.\n- After registry visibility waits, Sigstore repeatedly reports certificate SAN mismatch: expected that SHA-qualified identity, observed `https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/.github/workflows/daily-release.yml@refs/heads/main`. Verification exhausts retries.\n\n## Source and intended contract\nAt [20aeec scripts/release-continuation.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/blob/20aeecbd83f6d997576903c881940d459c9b5042/scripts/release-continuation.ts#L214-L221), continuation reads the **candidate preparation run**, validates its tooling SHA, and derives `signerWorkflow` from that run's referenced workflow path (only rewriting `@main`). The [workflow](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/blob/20aeecbd83f6d997576903c881940d459c9b5042/.github/workflows/daily-release.yml) forwards this as the publication verifier's signer expectation.\n[verify-registry-provenance.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/blob/20aeecbd83f6d997576903c881940d459c9b5042/scripts/verify-registry-provenance.ts) accepts the supplied identity and [release-provenance.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/blob/20aeecbd83f6d997576903c881940d459c9b5042/release-provenance.ts#L84-L90) enforces its exact SAN. Both verifier files were fetched at 831a0f and20aeec and are byte-identical; this is an identity-input mismatch, not evidence that the verifier should relax its check.\n\nCanonical [ops-release-continuation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/blob/20aeecbd83f6d997576903c881940d459c9b5042/.agents/pm/issues/ops-release-continuation.toon) requires exact candidate/artifact/run/config bindings, cryptographic provenance, authenticated reusable signer, and independent certificate source repository/merged commit/ref checks. Preparation tool provenance and the signer of a later publication are distinct facts.\n\n## Registry evidence and limits\nRead-only official npm metadata confirms version2026.11.11 and shasum `8be7e6fbd0bde5833202239e04d506b83ce79fd2`, matching the publish log; gitHead is absent.\n[Registry attestation](https://registry.npmjs.org/-/npm/v1/attestations/pm-ops@2026.11.11) decoded SLSA claims match the registry SHA512 subject, commit20aeec, caller release.yml@refs/heads/main and publication run43272393997/attempts/1. These decoded claims were **not independently cryptographically authenticated** in this review and are not authorization to trust the artifact. No package execution, live publication, recovery mutation, or security-setting change was performed.\n\nImpact: an accepted npm upload remains blocked at release completion/verification, despite registry visibility. Repeating the same identity comparison cannot fix it.\n\n## Acceptance / validation\n1. Keep candidate preparation tooling SHA binding independent from the authenticated publishing workflow identity.\n2. Resolve signer identity from authoritative evidence for the actual publication attempt, handling local reusable workflows and SHA-pinned external calls correctly.\n3. Preserve fail-closed signature, transparency/trust-root, exact signer identity, certificate source repo/merged commit/ref, and subject digest checks. Do not trust decoded claims or broadly accept arbitrary refs.\n4. Add regression coverage for preparation at831a0f followed by local reusable publication at20aeec/main; distinguish preparation pin, publishing workflow ref and implementation SHA.\n5. Negative controls must still reject foreign signer/repository/commit/ref, altered digest/signature and missing/ambiguous run metadata. Include recovery of already-published versions without duplicate publication.\n6. Validate against this read-only historical run/attestation and a cryptographically verified fixture; report fixture versus hosted evidence separately.\n\nDeduplication: all-status issues/PRs checked. #268 (sticky approval diagnosis) and #269 (candidate receipt parser) are distinct. Related original implementation #249/#250; this reports the concrete publication identity failure, not a duplicate capacity issue.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-12T19:44:12Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-ops#250 - Free release runners while protected PR checks run [closed]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!"
